      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Okay, so I was told that this is normal since my ears etc are going out of focus. The problem is that those pictures were taken with max Aperture (and the Avatar is not gigantic, it's the normal Rexouium height), so there is no way for me to get my ears in to focus. \nI've requested a higher max Aperture in another canny before, so I really hope that it will be added.\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/1144-allow-higher-aperture-values-for-camera",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-10-24T06:11:08.530Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I've played around a bit with the camera today. When I looked at the pictures I've made with Focus / Depth of Field, I noticed that there is a weird ghosting effect at the end of the ears of my Avatar. It looks a bit like it's on every edge of the Avatar but it's mostly noticeable at the emissions.\nThis seems really weird to me and probably needs to be fixed.\nOn the images below you can see what I mean with a \"ghosting\" effect. This is also not world specific as you can see the same effect in the last picture.",
